-- a definition of the library has a type, both given as code. The checker gives a λ a type only
-- against one expected, and a definition that calls another has that one's code, a λ, where it
-- is called; so the body checked is the machine's normal form of the translation: the definition
-- is checked as what it computes to. What a call drops is therefore not checked, and a body
-- whose normal form is not reached in the steps given is read as the machine left it (what the
-- checker then says of that was not established). Carrying each definition's type beside its
-- code would check a call as a call; a definition's type as code is not obtainable in this module
nk-code-has : Code → Code → Bool
nk-code-has t ty = nk-has (nk-nf (toNat #30000) (nk-of-code (toNat #200) t)) (nk-of-code (toNat #200) ty)
